* — `channel_mode % 4` makes it dead; retained.\n- **`0xFFF8U << 16`** typed as `u32` (`0xFFF80000`), matching C's `unsigned int` promotion.\n\n## Verification\n\nSymbol diff is empty in **both** directions — Rust exports exactly `update_frame_header`, nothing more, nothing less.\n\nI then built a `dlopen` differential harness loading the C and Rust `.so` side by side and comparing the **entire 24-byte struct** with `memcmp` (so stray writes to neighbouring fields would be caught too), pre-filling padding with `0xAA`/`0x5A`:\n\n- Exhaustive cross-product of hand-picked boundary values (every named case plus off-by-one neighbours, `0`, and `UINT32_MAX`): 42 blocksizes × 32 sample rates × 13 channel counts × 14 bit depths × 14 channel modes\n- Plus 3,000,000 xorshift-fuzzed iterations across the full 32-bit input space\n\n```\nsizeof(struct tflac)=24 align=4\ncases=6424512 mismatches=0\n```\n\n6.42 million cases, zero mismatches, plus a verified clean-slate `cargo clean && cargo build --release`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":24912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":735,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c14b497-0d5d-4450-a57c-41a01b41f949","uuid":"1d94419e-416a-46ac-b728-ebe5f7713c8c","timestamp":"2026-08-19T10:34:07.644Z"}
